 "notes": "NASDUCK SERF comagnetometer (K-3He). Headline result: first reliable terrestrial 95% C.L. bound on the ALP-proton coupling g_aPP (Fig. 2 right panel, protons.pdf vector figure from the e-print). The paper also bounds g_aNN (neutrons, left panel); the proton bound is the one the abstract highlights as novel. Extracted the black 'mean' line (binned log-log average of the dense jagged bound at 0.1% mass resolution); the true bound fluctuates around this within the plotted 1-sigma band. Axis calibration from major tick marks; cross-check: curve minimum 4.7e-6 GeV^-1 near 1.3e-11 eV matches the abstract's quoted closing of the 5e-6 to 2e-5 GeV^-1 region. Converted the paper's g_aPP [GeV^-1] (L = g \u2202_mu a p-bar gamma^mu gamma_5 p convention, cf. H = g_I grad(a)\u00b7I with epsilon_P=0.16 proton spin fraction of 39K) to the canonical dimensionless coupling via g_ap = 2 m_p g_aPP, m_p = 0.938 GeV. Two clipped points at the figure boundary (lowest masses, g>0.5 GeV^-1) were dropped. DM density: not stated explicitly; the paper assumes the Standard Halo Model of Lee et al. (2013) \u2014 0.4 GeV/cm^3 recorded as the presumed value. Precise tabulated bounds are on the collaboration's GitHub (not consulted).",
